## Now

# Two maintainers, and what is still lopsided

<div class="tiles">
<div class="tile h"><b>2</b><span>active maintainers, both admins and both in <code>@tutors-sdk/maintainers</code> (CODEOWNERS)</span></div>
<div class="tile h"><b>55 / 45</b><span>non-merge commits since June: 191 and 155</span></div>
<div class="tile h"><b>52 of 60</b><span>merges since 15 Sep by the second maintainer; 0 of 112 before</span></div>
</div>

<div class="cols">
<div class="card f">

### Honest reading
- **71%** of maintainer PRs (109 of 153) were merged by their own author
- Only **10 reviews** across 172 merged PRs, **8 of them from bots**
- Merge duty swung rather than split
- The org lists 5 admins; **2** have committed in the last 12 months

</div>
<div class="card h">

### What stands in for review
- A CI gate of 46 jobs (`ci-success`)
- **Ratchets** that refuse to let debt grow
- The **release harness** judging every candidate
- Two keyholders: either can merge, and the release runbook is written down

</div>
</div>

